# Bug reporting workflow

When the **user reports a bug** (in chat, Council, or as a task):

## 1. Repo board (source of truth)

Edit **`BUGS.md`** at repo root:

```markdown
## Open

- [ ] **Short title** — one-line repro or surface (e.g. Database → Gods)

## Investigating

(use when actively debugging)
```

- Use `- [ ] **Title**` format so vault sync picks it up.
- Move to **Fixed** when shipped; one line on what was wrong.

## 2. Vault mirror (Obsidian)

After editing `BUGS.md`, run:

```bash
npm run vault:sync
```

This refreshes:
- `Vault/Kanban/Bugs board.md`
- `Vault/_generated/open-bugs.md`
- **Dataview Dashboard** bug queries

Optional: deep-dive note from **`Vault/Templates/Bug investigation`** → save under `Vault/3-Resources/Bugs/`.

## 3. Council panel

If the bug came from a Council convene, also run:

```bash
npm run council:write-bug "Title — repro hint"
```

That appends `BUGS.md`, runs `vault:sync`, and posts a **MOD LOG** line in the Council chat.

## 4. Agent order

1. Read existing **BUGS.md** — avoid duplicates; merge related reports.
2. Add open item under **## Open** (or **Investigating** if you're starting now).
3. **`npm run vault:sync`**
4. Fix the bug before new features (see `agent-workflow.mdc`).

## Do not

- Log bugs only in chat or Vault without updating **BUGS.md**
- Skip vault sync after board changes the user should see in Obsidian
